XR presentation: the diorama's eyes masked by the table, its HUD on a panel of its own

For WakerQuest's diorama (patch 0025):
- Draws are marked at record time when the view delta (patch 0019) applies to them (DrawData.worldView,
  the world). In a diorama frame the eyes draw the world alone; after the right eye a third replay
  draws everything else (the HUD, the 2D, the menus) over a transparent EFB (stereo::encode_hud: its
  clears transparent, no texture copies, resolves, snapshots or encoder tasks), for a panel.
- Each eye is masked right after it is drawn, while its depth is in the EFB (stereo::encode_mask): a
  pass puts each pixel's point in the table's space (aurora_xr_set_diorama_mask: table from head,
  the frustum, the eye's shift, the fade) and writes alpha 0 outside the table's box (x and z within
  +-1, above the cut at -1), fading at its edges.
- The XR buffer is three eyes wide: the masked left and right eyes and the HUD (AuroraXrFrame.hud),
  copied with their alpha (straight). ImGui goes into a texture of the window's size and over the
  HUD's third. A diorama frame is always in stereo.

